> In the deprecation we mentioned to use the `Symfony\Component\Form\ChoiceList\Loader\LazyChoiceLoader`, which imply to use Symfony Form 7.2. Since this version is compatible with Symfony packages 6.4 ([symfony/form@`7.2`/composer.json](https://github.com/symfony/form/blob/7.2/composer.json?rgh-link-date=2025-09-25T07%3A04%3A51Z)), we could bump requirements (and add an explicit dependency on `symfony/form`, since the feature is not optional AFAIK?)

Finally I went for another solution. Since the `BaseEntityAutocompleteType` is only registered as a service when `symfony/form` is available, I added a check that throws an exception if `LazyChoiceLoader` does not exist, telling the user to install Symfony Form >= 7.2.
